    <!-- Settings: ping -->
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_116">PING TYPE</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_117">Stability</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_118">Moon Ping, TCP and HTTP answer the question &quot;is something listening on the port&quot;. That is not the same as &quot;the protocol works&quot;: a CDN, your provider's middlebox or a stale key will all complete a handshake, and a dead server will show a cheerful 30 ms.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_119">Stability is the only method that opens a real connection and makes a request through it. Slower than the rest, and it does not lie: if nothing comes back, no traffic will get through that server either.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_120">PROBE ORDER</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_121">Probe one at a time</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_122">Spread the probes out instead of firing them all at once. Some providers take a volley of thirty connections for a port scan and throttle it.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_123">Gap between probes</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_124">50 ms</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_125">150 ms</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_126">300 ms</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_127">AUTO-CHECK</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_128">Re-measures in the background so the numbers are fresh when you open the list.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_129">Off</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_130">1 min</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_131">5 min</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_132">10 min</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_133">15 min</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_134">20 min</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_135">30 min</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_136">PING DISPLAY</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_137">Numbers</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_138">Bars</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_139">Both</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_140">Dots</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_141">TEST URL</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_142">Presets</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_143">Used by HTTP GET / HEAD. Moon Ping and TCP probe the server itself.</s:String>
