    <!-- Settings: privacy -->
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_167">Moon Internet is a local VPN client. Below is how the app handles your data.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_168">We collect nothing</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_169">The app runs on your device. The developer receives none of your data: no accounts, no telemetry, no analytics, no phoning home.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_170">Data on your device</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_171">Subscriptions, the server list, keys and access passwords are kept locally in the app's folder (the &quot;save&quot; folder) and never leave your computer. Uninstalling the app removes them.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_172">Your traffic</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_173">Traffic goes through servers you added yourself, from your own subscription link. Their operators handle it under their own rules — read their policy. The app itself neither logs your traffic nor forwards it anywhere.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_174">Network requests</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_175">The app contacts only: (1) your subscription URLs, to fetch the server list; (2) the geo-rule sources such as GitHub, to download routing files when routing is on. Nowhere else.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_176">Logs</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_177">Technical logs for diagnosing a connection are kept locally and never uploaded. You can open them under &quot;Logs&quot;.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_178">Privileges</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_179">TUN mode needs administrator rights (the system tunnel service). It exists only to route traffic and collects nothing.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_180">Changes</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="S_SettingsView_181">This policy may be updated along with the app.</s:String>

